Power off and restart with the system's commands without logind/ConsoleKit.

The greeter's shut-down and restart buttons go through liblightdm-gobject,
which only knows logind and ConsoleKit over the system bus.  A system with
neither (LikeOS) had no way to power off from the login screen: both
lightdm_get_can_shutdown() and lightdm_get_can_restart() said no.

When neither service answers, the library now falls back to /bin/poweroff
and /bin/reboot: available when they are installed, and run (waited for,
with their exit status checked) to act.  They decide themselves whom they
act for -- on LikeOS root and the user logged in at the console, which the
greeter's user is while the greeter runs.  Suspend and hibernate keep
saying no.

